  "self_load_only": true,
  "description": "bigville: N-INPUT + Y-TOOL CATALOG-RECIPE PRODUCTION in the living economy (goods port step 2+3). be_meet_input/be_recipe_done/be_reset_input port the rich an_meet/an_done checklist -- a shop produces via its real CATALOG recipe, consuming ALL N inputs (all-or-nothing) then minting output proportional to skill. be_recipe_done also requires every required TOOL to be working (Y-tools, generalising be_print's press-gate: a worn-out tool blocks the batch) and be_wear_tool wears each tool once per batch until it breaks. Distinct make_armed flag; be_produce untouched. The catalog's recipes -- inputs AND tools -- now drive living production. be_composite_quality sets a made good's quality (condition) to its WEAKEST input part -- composite quality = weakest link, reusing condition (which wear/spoilage already drive).",
