    {
      "name": "be_recipe_done",
      "batch": false,
      "comment": "When all N recipe inputs are met AND every required TOOL is working (Y-tools, be_print's press-gate generalised -- a worn-out tool blocks the batch), the make-armed shop mints output = the recipe's batch size (out_qty) * skill, bumps make_count (so tools wear once per batch), and disarms. A shop with no inputs/tools completes at once. Requires the keeper CONSCIOUS (not collapsed/asleep) -- you cannot work the forge while unconscious (a world fact, like be_produce). PHYSICAL DEMAND: the keeper's BODY must be strong enough (strength >= shop.strength_req -- a heavy trade you cannot do if too weak) AND have enough stamina reserve (>= shop.stamina_cost); completing the batch SPENDS that stamina from the reserve (rest restores it). Default 0/0 -> light trades unaffected. Working a heavy recipe also makes the keeper HUNGRIER (hunger_level += stamina_cost*HUNGER_PER_STAMINA) -- exertion needs more food; feeds the same hunger the sale/drive use.",
