    {
      "name": "be_composite_quality",
      "batch": false,
      "comment": "COMPOSITE QUALITY = WEAKEST PART: after a batch, the made good's quality (condition) is set to the MINIMUM condition among its inputs -- `weakest` is the input no other is below. A chain is only as strong as its weakest link: a cart from a worn wheel is a worn cart. Epoch-guarded on make_count (once per batch); a 0-input raw producer has no has_input so keeps full quality. Coheres with wear/spoilage -- condition IS the good's quality/state. CONTAMINATION: the result is min(current pile, weakest input) -- adding fresh stock to a degraded pile cannot refresh it (the fresh is dragged down), so a continuously-restocked perishable still ages and rots.",
      "match": [
        [
          "shop",
          "stocks",
          "stock"
        ],
        [
          "shop",
          "has_input",
          "weakest"
        ]
      ],
